  <!-- One output root for every variant: out\<Platform>\<Configuration>\ for the
       binaries, with the compiler's intermediates tucked under obj\ inside it.
       Both are pinned unconditionally and anchored on $(ProjectDir), because the
       MSBuild defaults are neither stable nor tidy:
         - OutDir defaulted to $(SolutionDir)$(Platform)\$(Configuration)\, so the
           linked DLL moved depending on which solution drove the build.
         - IntDir defaulted to $(ShortProjectName)\$(Platform)\$(Configuration)\
           when SolutionDir was this project's own folder and to
           $(Platform)\$(Configuration)\ otherwise, which is how the old x64\Debug
           held intermediates but no DLL while a stray Targetcore\x64\Debug held
           the rest.
       Everything downstream is path-independent and needs no change: the deploy
       CustomBuildStep reads $(TargetDir), and the import library goes to
       $(WDMSCS_LIB) (MSCS\lib\<Platform>\<Configuration>) via Directory.Build.props. -->

  <!-- <Inputs>$(TargetPath) on every CustomBuildStep below. Without an input
       naming the binary being copied, MSBuild compares the staged DLL against
       this .vcxproj alone and skips the deploy, so the shared bin\<Cfg><Arch>
       tree serves a stale DLL against a freshly written import library.

       The metadata NAME is the whole fix. This was added 2026-08-22 as
       <AdditionalInputs> and changed nothing, because Microsoft.CppCommon.targets
       declares the step as

         <Target Name="CustomBuildStep"
                 Inputs="%(CustomBuildStep.Inputs);$(ProjectFileName)" ...>

       and nothing folds AdditionalInputs into that - the name belongs to the
       per-file CustomBuild item, not to the project-level build step, so the
       value was simply inert metadata. Symptom: an up-to-date skip that no
       relink ever clears. -v:diag -t:CustomBuildStep names the input set, and
       prints "Input files: Targetcore(2026).vcxproj" alone when it is wrong.

       The matching comment in Msgcore\Msgcore(2026).vcxproj carries the same
       correction - the two projects had the same defect, and the same fix. -->
